<decompilertest>
<!--
    Kuna #1626: on AArch64 the memory-tagging instructions lost their tag
    effect, and barriers and hints printed under their SLEIGH instruction
    names.  AARCH64.pspec leaves the ShowMemTag context at 0, under which
    irg/addg/subg/gmi/ldg lift as a pointer copy or add and stg/st2g as
    nothing, so `return __arm_mte_create_random_tag(p, 0);` decompiled to
    `return a0;` and `__arm_mte_set_tag(p)` to an empty `void f(void)`.

    Stage / sub-stage: P9 naming-policy (`option acleintrinsics`, AArch64
    only, default on), with a P2 context paint (`kuna_memtag`).  On sets
    ShowMemTag to 1 before a function is lifted, so each tag instruction is
    one user op whose result is the tagged pointer, and
    `kuna_acleintrinsics` prints the barrier, hint and tag user ops as the
    ACLE intrinsics of <arm_acle.h>, recombining a barrier's domain and
    type operands into the 4-bit CRm.

    First chunk: clang 22 -O2 for aarch64-linux-gnu with
    -march=armv8.5-a+memtag over
      void barrier(volatile int *p) { *p = 1; __dmb(11); __dsb(15); __isb(15); }
      void idle(void) { __wfi(); __yield(); __wfe(); __sev(); __sevl(); }
      void *tag(void *p) { return __arm_mte_create_random_tag(p, 0); }
      void *inc(void *p) { return __arm_mte_increment_tag(p, 3); }
      unsigned long excl(void *p, unsigned long m) { return __arm_mte_exclude_tag(p, m); }
      void settag(void *p) { __arm_mte_set_tag(p); }
      void *gettag(void *p) { return __arm_mte_get_tag(p); }
      void *alloc16(void *p) { void *q = __arm_mte_create_random_tag(p,
          __arm_mte_exclude_tag(p, 0)); __arm_mte_set_tag(q); return q; }
    Second chunk, hand-assembled shapes no intrinsic produces:
      store_other  stg x1,[x0]; ret        store_pair  st2g x0,[x0],#32; ret
      load_other   ldg x1,[x0]; mov x0,x1; ret
      add_off      addg x0,x0,#32,#1; ret  sub_off     subg x0,x1,#16,#2; ret
      isb_one      isb #1; ret             clear2      stzg x0,[x0]; ret

    Pass 1 (option acleintrinsics off): the output before this option.
    Pass 2 (default): the intrinsics; a tag load or store whose pointer is
    not its own granule address keeps its user-op name.
-->
