<stringmatch name="ACLE #1: off, a tagging function returns its argument unchanged" min="3" max="3">^\s*return a0;$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="ACLE #2: off, barriers print under their SLEIGH names" min="4" max="4">DataMemoryBarrier\(2,3\);|DataSynchronizationBarrier\(3,3,0\);|InstructionSynchronizationBarrier\(\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="ACLE #3: off, hints print under their SLEIGH names" min="5" max="5">WaitForInterrupt\(\);|Yield\(\);|WaitForEvent\(\);|SendEvent\(\);|SendEventLocally\(\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="ACLE #4: irg is a call that produces the returned pointer" min="1" max="1">^\s*return __arm_mte_create_random_tag\(a0,0\);$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="ACLE #5: barriers print with their CRm recombined" min="3" max="3">^\s*__dmb\(11\);$|^\s*__dsb\(15\);$|^\s*__isb\(15\);$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="ACLE #6: the isb option comes from the instruction" min="1" max="1">^\s*__isb\(1\);$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="ACLE #7: hints print as intrinsics" min="5" max="5">^\s*__wfi\(\);$|^\s*__yield\(\);$|^\s*__wfe\(\);$|^\s*__sev\(\);$|^\s*__sevl\(\);$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="ACLE #8: addg and subg increment the tag of the moved pointer" min="3" max="3">return __arm_mte_increment_tag\(a0,3\);|return __arm_mte_increment_tag\(a0 \+ 0x20,1\);|return __arm_mte_increment_tag\(a1 \+ -0x10,2\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="ACLE #9: gmi and ldg produce their results" min="2" max="2">return __arm_mte_exclude_tag\(a0,a1\);|return __arm_mte_get_tag\(a0\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="ACLE #10: a pointer tagging its own granule is __arm_mte_set_tag" min="4" max="4">^\s*__arm_mte_set_tag\((a0|v1)\);$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="ACLE #11: the tagged pointer flows from irg through stg to the return" min="1" max="1">v1 = __arm_mte_create_random_tag\(a0,__arm_mte_exclude_tag\(a0,0\)\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="ACLE #12: a tag store or load of another granule keeps its user-op name" min="3" max="3">^\s*StorePtrTag\(a0,a1\);$|^\s*StorePtrTag\(a0 \+ 0x10,a0\);$|return LoadPtrTag\(a1,a0\);</stringmatch>
